# shir_nodes/field_read.node — FieldRead: named field read on a composite
# VALUE (struct literal field access: `p.x` where p = Point { x: 1, .. }).
#
# GENERIC. object is any expression evaluating to a record/object value;
# name is the plain field ident. Tuple-index reads (`p.0`) are NOT this
# node — they keep refusing until a tuple contract lands. Named-variable
# struct storage keeps existing A1 shapes; THIS node covers the
# expression-position form frontends previously had no shape for.
# Numeric NAMES ("0", "1" on tuples) render COMPUTED access
# (JS obj[0], Perl $obj->[0]) — the name is then an INDEX.
# Backends: JS obj.name / obj[0] (native MemberExpression),
# Perl $obj->{name} / $obj->[0].

node FieldRead
tag "FieldRead"
kind expr
# storage_class str_bounded
field object: expr
field name: string
# Spec: TextOps#field_read_sound (docs/fm/TextOps/ShIR_TextOps_Strings.thy, section
# "ReadLine, ElementRead, FieldRead, TypeAssert: readback laws"). A field read is an
# element read with the field name's bytes as the query — the two nodes are one function
# at two spellings, which is proved — so the readback law is the same: reading a name
# that occurs LAST in a literal yields that last value (duplicates read back last-wins).
#
# NOT PROMISED (stated, not assumed): the key-stringification rule (abstract st);
# property order; the renderer's rule that a NUMERIC name is an INDEX (`obj[0]`,
# `$obj->[0]`) rather than a lookup, which is a rendering decision outside this law;
# tuple-index reads, which this node explicitly does not cover; and the missing-key
# policy.
spec: TextOps#field_read_sound
